From 897e8085ea5cbced22bd801e5cc26f20a4fdaf05 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:42:44 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] A rope can run from a unit's hand to a spot or to another
 unit, following the hand

A grappling hook's line was invisible: the pull read as a jump with nothing holding it (Corey's
review of Grapple Arrow and Harpoon Dive; Reverse Grapple's haul had no line either). A placed
object can't follow a hero flying through the air, so SetUnitRope(key, unit, x, y, z, seconds[,
colour]) draws a taut rope from the unit's right hand to that spot, from where the hand is each
frame; with another unit's guid in place of the spot it runs to that unit's chest. A strip facing
the camera, a darker rim either side of a lighter tan core, depth-tested, never darker than half
its colour so it reads at night. ClearUnitRope([key]). HasActionCombat() is 21.
